---
title: Chapter 14: Circular Procurement and Asset Stewardship
---
flowchart TD
 S1["1. Translate service needs into lifecycle procurement criteria\nSpecify durability, modularity, repairability, interoperability, support, take-back, and data requirements."]
 S2["2. Assess the current asset and dependencies\nReview condition, remaining life, software support, cybersecurity, validation, workload, downtime, and supply chain."]
 S1 --> S2
 S3["3. Compare maintain, repair, refurbish, replace, and share options\nUse the same service requirement, horizon, safety constraints, and cost boundary."]
 S2 --> S3
 S4["4. Validate safety, regulatory, quality, and continuity conditions\nConfirm infection prevention, device requirements, data erasure, recipient due diligence, and fallback."]
 S3 --> S4
 S5["5. Contract for support, residual value, and end of life\nDefine components, updates, take-back, recovery evidence, pricing, remedies, and exit."]
 S4 --> S5
 S6["6. Implement the selected option\nPlan transition, training, downtime, testing, communication, and monitoring."]
 S5 --> S6
 S7["7. Decommission and close responsibly\nPreserve records, erase data, maintain chain of custody, verify disposition, and recognize residual or recovery value."]
 S6 --> S7
